/-!
# Unitary-five calculations for the Green Book reduction

The concrete line parabolic has a nontrivial normal two-subgroup and odd-prime
rank at least three whenever the even prime-power parameter differs from four.
Its embedding in a quasithin completion therefore forces the parameter four;
this also excludes every extension of the U₅(2) amalgam. No rank or normal-core
calculation remains as an assumption of these exclusion theorems.

At parameter four the source groups L₁ and L₂ are the embedded parabolic
residuals. Their canonical two-core quotients are the actual SU₃(4) and
PSL₂(16) matrix groups. The first core is special of order 4⁷ with center
order four, and the second has order 2¹⁶. The common Sylow subgroup, source
Borel products, centralizing label and both amalgam inclusion maps are
identified with the concrete flag marking. These are the unitary-five
calculations used in F.1.12; exhaustive recognition remains a separate theorem.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
F.1.12, printed pp. 263--264; compare A.2.18, printed p. 40.
-/
